{"parentUuid":"f1718801-5387-4c7f-996d-2839fce9c1c1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgiz7BDDdW6BVQkncsZqr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1455,"cache_read_input_tokens":214022,"output_tokens":955,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":139},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1455,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":955,"cache_read_input_tokens":214022,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1455,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1455},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":7723,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"4a6aa3fe-4d76-4cd0-8e1b-dfa407b24737","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cgiz7AvrVSug7XNFNn54U","requestRef":"ea487d9d-6d83-43a1-a138-a32c8cae9968","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"da9678a5-d029-4beb-8a8f-01668898e01a","timestamp":"2026-11-05T02:23:15.445Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc","sessionId":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","version":"2.1.317","gitBranch":"ec-ai-corpus","slug":"calm-crunching-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"da9678a5-d029-4beb-8a8f-01668898e01a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgiz7BDDdW6BVQkncsZqr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've built a working prototype of the badges: `~/tray/argument-check-badges.html`.\n\nEvery badge comes from the real check output, not typed numbers. Two runs gave identical bytes, and I opened it in headless Chrome to check the layout. The page is built at commit 7a8ebf5, which another session committed after my last push.\n\n**What's on it:**\n- **Five badges for the paper:**\n  - `argument | thesis fails`\n  - `quotes | 74/97 found`\n  - `premises | 5 unsourced`\n  - `argument steps | 3/15 stand`\n  - `build | 7a8ebf5 · check 4c2e32b56e8a`\n- **Four example claim badges**, such as `Q094 | ok · carries 5` and `A03 | fails · carries 3`. \"carries N\" is the number of claims that rest on this one, a first simple version of because-ness. Q094 carries 5: A02c, A02, A09, T0 and R0.\n- **Hover text:** each badge has a title that also works for screen readers. For example, the premises badge's title names the five premises: A02a, A02b, A02d, A03 and A04.\n\n**Your \"this is what I think\" case needs a second kind of badge.** There are two:\n- **A live badge** works like a CI badge. It shows today's result and changes as the record changes, so it belongs in a README.\n- **A pinned badge** is fixed to a commit and the digest of the check output (`Q094@1abaa3d`). It never changes, and clicking it opens that exact version. That makes it a citation: you can drop it in a post and it still says what the claim rested on when you made it, even after the record moves.\n\n**Rules I gave them:**\n- computed, never typed;\n- the state is always spelled out in words, never shown by colour alone;\n- if the check can't run, the badge says \"unverified\" rather than showing an old pass.\n\n**Not built yet:**\n- **The click-through pages.** Each claim's page would show its quote, source, page and digest, what it rests on, and everything that rests on it. These are the primitive pages again; for now the prototype only names where a click would go.\n- **The generator for real.** The prototype is a throwaway script in my scratch folder, not committed. The real generator only reads the check output, so it belongs in Descartes as something like `descartes badge`.\n\nTwo decisions for you:\n- **Hosting:** GitHub Pages, release assets, or the Praxis site.\n- **Which badges to offer:** the paper set, a badge per claim, or both."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1455,"cache_read_input_tokens":214022,"output_tokens":955,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":139},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1455,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":955,"cache_read_input_tokens":214022,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1455,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1455},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"4a6aa3fe-4d76-4cd0-8e1b-dfa407b24737","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cgiz7AvrVSug7XNFNn54U","requestRef":"ea487d9d-6d83-43a1-a138-a32c8cae9968","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"dd1eceef-94c7-43f0-8645-e05064bf1544","timestamp":"2026-11-05T02:23:16.384Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc","sessionId":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","version":"2.1.317","gitBranch":"ec-ai-corpus","slug":"calm-crunching-lovelace"}
