{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","id":"e60be7e3-afa5-4c1b-b9a5-0e9558c1012e","timestamp":"2026-11-05T02:32:28.023Z","version":"2.1.317","querySource":"repl_main_thread","shapeHash":"abdbf879f1c8baf4d3d130a8ccbe0672e594508c87565d961c1f493173127f1f","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"ec57889e-6894-4313-ba74-faec9684a995","keep":142,"tail":["51902559d57f1aeba5ce5582cb2668fce2c089f867945450fb820c27c67cff73","48d6988fe829811d120841925ab73fba81ec68bdd80a4666320367c11ebf32dc"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",143,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"f799f1943c39fd8eb0058e2b38e467f526cae22672b71c889686335427dd671c"}
{"type":"file-history-delta","messageId":"d7a3a7b7-3c33-4a7d-8511-38511e3c140a","snapshotMessageId":"e2d6da9d-344f-4448-87c3-f84df8bd98ad","trackingPath":"docs/badges.md","backup":{"backupFileName":null,"version":1,"backupTime":"2026-11-05T02:32:42.460Z","realParentDir":"/Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc/docs"},"timestamp":"2026-11-05T02:32:42.462Z"}
{"parentUuid":"5ccb1c52-8d13-483d-b499-efb728610024","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgizpXEsN8doC1Xh1nf7o","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NnwpGTBQ2njqXT5w8hfvXD","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc/docs/badges.md","content":"# Badges: citations last, status expires\n\nA badge is a small image of a check result that someone can embed and click\nthrough. There are two kinds, with opposite duties (Sloane, 2026-11-04).\n\n## Citation badges are durable\n\nA citation badge says *this is what I think, and here is exactly what it\nrested on when I said it.* It must outlive its host, its links and the\nrepository's later history.\n\n- **Pinned.** It names one commit and never changes. A later result gets a\n  new badge; the old one stays true about its moment.\n- **Self-contained.** The badge file carries its full reference in its own\n  `<metadata>`: the document, repository and commit; the claim, its statement,\n  witness and `rests_on`; the quote; the source (id, URL, fetch date, bytes,\n  BLAKE3); the text it was checked in (path, recipe, SHA-256, offset); the\n  checker binary's SHA-256; the SHA-256 of the full check output; and the\n  command that re-verifies it. With every link dead, the file alone is enough\n  to check it.\n- **Content-addressed.** Its file name is `<claim>@<commit>-<digest>.svg`,\n  where the digest is of the badge itself, so a copy can be checked against\n  its name.\n- **Deterministic.** The same commit and check output give the same bytes.\n\n## Status badges expire\n\nA status badge says *where this stands now.* Now ends, so the badge must too.\n\n- **Dated on its face.** The visible text includes the date of the check it\n  shows, so a screenshot dates itself.\n- **Valid for a stated window.** After the window the host serves an\n  expired badge that says *stale, recheck* in words and claims nothing. It\n  never falls back to the last pass.\n- **Unverified if the check can't run.** No result means no claim.\n- **Time is an argument.** The as-of date and the window are recorded inputs,\n  never read from a clock inside the generator (AGENTS.md, \"Deterministic\").\n\n## Both kinds\n\n- **Words, not just colour.** Every badge spells out its state (\"fails\",\n  \"ok\", \"5 unsourced\", \"stale\").\n- **Computed, never typed.** A badge is a pure function of the claims file\n  and the check output.\n- **Clicks through** to the claim's page: statement, quote, source, what it\n  rests on and what rests on it.\n- **Belongs in Descartes.** The generator reads only the check output, so the\n  real one is a Rust command beside `check`. The prototype\n  (`~/tray/argument-check-badges.html`, 2026-11-04) was a throwaway script.\n\n## Open\n\n- The status window (the prototype used one day).\n- Hosting for status badges and claim pages.\n- Signing citation badges, once there's a key (Praxis `OPENQUESTIONS.md` Q1).\n- Whether the badge schema becomes a Praxis-wide contract.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1056,"cache_read_input_tokens":220282,"output_tokens":1477,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1056,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1477,"cache_read_input_tokens":220282,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1056,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1056},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01NnwpGTBQ2njqXT5w8hfvXD":{"file_path":"/Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc/docs/badges.md","content":"# Badges: citations last, status expires\n\nA badge is a small image of a check result that someone can embed and click\nthrough. There are two kinds, with opposite duties (Sloane, 2026-11-04).\n\n## Citation badges are durable\n\nA citation badge says *this is what I think, and here is exactly what it\nrested on when I said it.* It must outlive its host, its links and the\nrepository's later history.\n\n- **Pinned.** It names one commit and never changes. A later result gets a\n  new badge; the old one stays true about its moment.\n- **Self-contained.** The badge file carries its full reference in its own\n  `<metadata>`: the document, repository and commit; the claim, its statement,\n  witness and `rests_on`; the quote; the source (id, URL, fetch date, bytes,\n  BLAKE3); the text it was checked in (path, recipe, SHA-256, offset); the\n  checker binary's SHA-256; the SHA-256 of the full check output; and the\n  command that re-verifies it. With every link dead, the file alone is enough\n  to check it.\n- **Content-addressed.** Its file name is `<claim>@<commit>-<digest>.svg`,\n  where the digest is of the badge itself, so a copy can be checked against\n  its name.\n- **Deterministic.** The same commit and check output give the same bytes.\n\n## Status badges expire\n\nA status badge says *where this stands now.* Now ends, so the badge must too.\n\n- **Dated on its face.** The visible text includes the date of the check it\n  shows, so a screenshot dates itself.\n- **Valid for a stated window.** After the window the host serves an\n  expired badge that says *stale, recheck* in words and claims nothing. It\n  never falls back to the last pass.\n- **Unverified if the check can't run.** No result means no claim.\n- **Time is an argument.** The as-of date and the window are recorded inputs,\n  never read from a clock inside the generator (AGENTS.md, \"Deterministic\").\n\n## Both kinds\n\n- **Words, not just colour.** Every badge spells out its state (\"fails\",\n  \"ok\", \"5 unsourced\", \"stale\").\n- **Computed, never typed.** A badge is a pure function of the claims file\n  and the check output.\n- **Clicks through** to the claim's page: statement, quote, source, what it\n  rests on and what rests on it.\n- **Belongs in Descartes.** The generator reads only the check output, so the\n  real one is a Rust command beside `check`. The prototype\n  (`~/tray/argument-check-badges.html`, 2026-11-04) was a throwaway script.\n\n## Open\n\n- The status window (the prototype used one day).\n- Hosting for status badges and claim pages.\n- Signing citation badges, once there's a key (Praxis `OPENQUESTIONS.md` Q1).\n- Whether the badge schema becomes a Praxis-wide contract.\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"af067095-a846-42a0-b249-185a93005d4a","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgizpX3UFAxiA1S97PuCH","requestRef":"e60be7e3-afa5-4c1b-b9a5-0e9558c1012e","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"d7a3a7b7-3c33-4a7d-8511-38511e3c140a","timestamp":"2026-11-05T02:32:38.525Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc","sessionId":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","version":"2.1.317","gitBranch":"ec-ai-corpus","slug":"calm-crunching-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"d7a3a7b7-3c33-4a7d-8511-38511e3c140a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgizpXEsN8doC1Xh1nf7o","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01U81D43uSd5pR99XJwCs3iy","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git add docs/badges.md && printf '%s\\n' \"Badges: citation badges are durable and self-contained; status badges expire\" \"\" \"Citation: pinned to a commit, full reference in the SVG's own metadata,\" \"content-addressed name, deterministic. Status: dated on its face, valid for\" \"a stated window, then 'stale, recheck'; never a cached pass. Prototype in\" \"the tray; the real generator belongs in Descartes.\" \"\" \"Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" > /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-srvo-dev-anthropic-pbc/c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475/scratchpad/msg9.txt && git commit -q -F /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-srvo-dev-anthropic-pbc/c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475/scratchpad/msg9.txt && git push -q origin ec-ai-corpus && git log --oneline -1","description":"Commit the badge standard and push"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1056,"cache_read_input_tokens":220282,"output_tokens":1477,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1056,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1477,"cache_read_input_tokens":220282,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1056,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1056},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01U81D43uSd5pR99XJwCs3iy":{"command":"cd /Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc && git add docs/badges.md && printf '%s\\n' \"Badges: citation badges are durable and self-contained; status badges expire\" \"\" \"Citation: pinned to a commit, full reference in the SVG's own metadata,\" \"content-addressed name, deterministic. Status: dated on its face, valid for\" \"a stated window, then 'stale, recheck'; never a cached pass. Prototype in\" \"the tray; the real generator belongs in Descartes.\" \"\" \"Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" > /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-srvo-dev-anthropic-pbc/c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475/scratchpad/msg9.txt && git commit -q -F /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-srvo-dev-anthropic-pbc/c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475/scratchpad/msg9.txt && git push -q origin ec-ai-corpus && git log --oneline -1","description":"Commit the badge standard and push"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01U81D43uSd5pR99XJwCs3iy":{"cwd":"/Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"af067095-a846-42a0-b249-185a93005d4a","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgizpX3UFAxiA1S97PuCH","requestRef":"e60be7e3-afa5-4c1b-b9a5-0e9558c1012e","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"b6e8a02a-b434-4f6c-b336-e8870f92c5be","timestamp":"2026-11-05T02:32:42.358Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc","sessionId":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","version":"2.1.317","gitBranch":"ec-ai-corpus","slug":"calm-crunching-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"d7a3a7b7-3c33-4a7d-8511-38511e3c140a","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"8051663f-0781-42a2-8356-5d2b3e1ace34","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NnwpGTBQ2njqXT5w8hfvXD","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc/docs/badges.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"6073ed10-c976-44cc-bf23-06820b10343b","timestamp":"2026-11-05T02:32:42.467Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc/docs/badges.md","content":"# Badges: citations last, status expires\n\nA badge is a small image of a check result that someone can embed and click\nthrough. There are two kinds, with opposite duties (Sloane, 2026-11-04).\n\n## Citation badges are durable\n\nA citation badge says *this is what I think, and here is exactly what it\nrested on when I said it.* It must outlive its host, its links and the\nrepository's later history.\n\n- **Pinned.** It names one commit and never changes. A later result gets a\n  new badge; the old one stays true about its moment.\n- **Self-contained.** The badge file carries its full reference in its own\n  `<metadata>`: the document, repository and commit; the claim, its statement,\n  witness and `rests_on`; the quote; the source (id, URL, fetch date, bytes,\n  BLAKE3); the text it was checked in (path, recipe, SHA-256, offset); the\n  checker binary's SHA-256; the SHA-256 of the full check output; and the\n  command that re-verifies it. With every link dead, the file alone is enough\n  to check it.\n- **Content-addressed.** Its file name is `<claim>@<commit>-<digest>.svg`,\n  where the digest is of the badge itself, so a copy can be checked against\n  its name.\n- **Deterministic.** The same commit and check output give the same bytes.\n\n## Status badges expire\n\nA status badge says *where this stands now.* Now ends, so the badge must too.\n\n- **Dated on its face.** The visible text includes the date of the check it\n  shows, so a screenshot dates itself.\n- **Valid for a stated window.** After the window the host serves an\n  expired badge that says *stale, recheck* in words and claims nothing. It\n  never falls back to the last pass.\n- **Unverified if the check can't run.** No result means no claim.\n- **Time is an argument.** The as-of date and the window are recorded inputs,\n  never read from a clock inside the generator (AGENTS.md, \"Deterministic\").\n\n## Both kinds\n\n- **Words, not just colour.** Every badge spells out its state (\"fails\",\n  \"ok\", \"5 unsourced\", \"stale\").\n- **Computed, never typed.** A badge is a pure function of the claims file\n  and the check output.\n- **Clicks through** to the claim's page: statement, quote, source, what it\n  rests on and what rests on it.\n- **Belongs in Descartes.** The generator reads only the check output, so the\n  real one is a Rust command beside `check`. The prototype\n  (`~/tray/argument-check-badges.html`, 2026-11-04) was a throwaway script.\n\n## Open\n\n- The status window (the prototype used one day).\n- Hosting for status badges and claim pages.\n- Signing citation badges, once there's a key (Praxis `OPENQUESTIONS.md` Q1).\n- Whether the badge schema becomes a Praxis-wide contract.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d7a3a7b7-3c33-4a7d-8511-38511e3c140a","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc","sessionId":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","version":"2.1.317","gitBranch":"ec-ai-corpus","slug":"calm-crunching-lovelace"}
