{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","hash":"a8e360dd33f3c7ae21effa2b8c135aa1d70602cc33457bf2f04867547a768b6a","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NnwpGTBQ2njqXT5w8hfvXD","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc/docs/badges.md","content":"# Badges: citations last, status expires\n\nA badge is a small image of a check result that someone can embed and click\nthrough. There are two kinds, with opposite duties (Sloane, 2026-11-04).\n\n## Citation badges are durable\n\nA citation badge says *this is what I think, and here is exactly what it\nrested on when I said it.* It must outlive its host, its links and the\nrepository's later history.\n\n- **Pinned.** It names one commit and never changes. A later result gets a\n  new badge; the old one stays true about its moment.\n- **Self-contained.** The badge file carries its full reference in its own\n  `<metadata>`: the document, repository and commit; the claim, its statement,\n  witness and `rests_on`; the quote; the source (id, URL, fetch date, bytes,\n  BLAKE3); the text it was checked in (path, recipe, SHA-256, offset); the\n  checker binary's SHA-256; the SHA-256 of the full check output; and the\n  command that re-verifies it. With every link dead, the file alone is enough\n  to check it.\n- **Content-addressed.** Its file name is `<claim>@<commit>-<digest>.svg`,\n  where the digest is of the badge itself, so a copy can be checked against\n  its name.\n- **Deterministic.** The same commit and check output give the same bytes.\n\n## Status badges expire\n\nA status badge says *where this stands now.* Now ends, so the badge must too.\n\n- **Dated on its face.** The visible text includes the date of the check it\n  shows, so a screenshot dates itself.\n- **Valid for a stated window.** After the window the host serves an\n  expired badge that says *stale, recheck* in words and claims nothing. It\n  never falls back to the last pass.\n- **Unverified if the check can't run.** No result means no claim.\n- **Time is an argument.** The as-of date and the window are recorded inputs,\n  never read from a clock inside the generator (AGENTS.md, \"Deterministic\").\n\n## Both kinds\n\n- **Words, not just colour.** Every badge spells out its state (\"fails\",\n  \"ok\", \"5 unsourced\", \"stale\").\n- **Computed, never typed.** A badge is a pure function of the claims file\n  and the check output.\n- **Clicks through** to the claim's page: statement, quote, source, what it\n  rests on and what rests on it.\n- **Belongs in Descartes.** The generator reads only the check output, so the\n  real one is a Rust command beside `check`. The prototype\n  (`~/tray/argument-check-badges.html`, 2026-11-04) was a throwaway script.\n\n## Open\n\n- The status window (the prototype used one day).\n- Hosting for status badges and claim pages.\n- Signing citation badges, once there's a key (Praxis `OPENQUESTIONS.md` Q1).\n- Whether the badge schema becomes a Praxis-wide contract.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01U81D43uSd5pR99XJwCs3iy","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc && git add docs/badges.md && printf '%s\\n' \"Badges: citation badges are durable and self-contained; status badges expire\" \"\" \"Citation: pinned to a commit, full reference in the SVG's own metadata,\" \"content-addressed name, deterministic. Status: dated on its face, valid for\" \"a stated window, then 'stale, recheck'; never a cached pass. Prototype in\" \"the tray; the real generator belongs in Descartes.\" \"\" \"Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" > /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-srvo-dev-anthropic-pbc/c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475/scratchpad/msg9.txt && git commit -q -F /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-srvo-dev-anthropic-pbc/c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475/scratchpad/msg9.txt && git push -q origin ec-ai-corpus && git log --oneline -1","description":"Commit the badge standard and push"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","id":"a88850ce-3332-4434-ad38-a1238da92f31","timestamp":"2026-11-05T02:32:46.835Z","version":"2.1.317","querySource":"repl_main_thread","shapeHash":"abdbf879f1c8baf4d3d130a8ccbe0672e594508c87565d961c1f493173127f1f","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"e60be7e3-afa5-4c1b-b9a5-0e9558c1012e","keep":144,"tail":["a8e360dd33f3c7ae21effa2b8c135aa1d70602cc33457bf2f04867547a768b6a","96d9baee7afb5683a93c7a1263f26772317c255bfe198aed319f243e98c589df"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",145,"content",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"3102fefd552ab71b7692376154b11fae97681a5da31bb1c0416b93af1d438b5c"}
{"parentUuid":"6c264dca-67c8-47b1-a8e5-b9577e7dd2fb","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01U81D43uSd5pR99XJwCs3iy","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"abc77d8f-32cc-45be-9c8d-fadb89d8ceff","timestamp":"2026-11-05T02:32:53.336Z","session_id":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc","sessionId":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","version":"2.1.317","gitBranch":"ec-ai-corpus","slug":"calm-crunching-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"abc77d8f-32cc-45be-9c8d-fadb89d8ceff","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgizquX77pFRS95M8dndV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written the two-kinds rule as a standard and built both kinds into the prototype. The standard is `docs/badges.md`, committed and pushed as `eaafc82`. The tray page `~/tray/argument-check-badges.html` now shows both kinds.\n\n**Citation badges last**\n- The example is `Q094@7a8ebf5-4ea2f8c6210a.svg`, a 2,760-byte SVG.\n- It carries its whole reference inside the file:\n  - the claim, its statement and the quote;\n  - the source's URL, fetch date, size and hash;\n  - the text it was checked in, with its hash and character position;\n  - the commit and the checker binary's hash;\n  - a hash of the full check output;\n  - the command that re-verifies it.\n\n  The page shows all of that data.\n- If every link to it dies, the file alone is still enough to check it.\n- The filename contains the badge's own digest, so a copy can be checked against its name.\n- Two generator runs produced the same file.\n\n**Status badges expire**\n- The date is printed on the badge itself, e.g. `thesis fails · as of 2026-11-04`, so even a screenshot is dated.\n- After its window, the host serves a grey `stale since … · recheck` badge that claims nothing. It never falls back to the last passing result.\n- If the check can't run, the badge says \"unverified\".\n- The date and the window are inputs to the generator, never read from a clock, so the bytes stay deterministic.\n\n**What's still open:**\n- **The status window.** The prototype uses one day; how long it should be is your call.\n- **Hosting.** Expiry only works if a host serves the stale version after the window. A static file on GitHub can't expire by itself, though the printed date still dates it.\n- **Signing citation badges.** This waits on the signing-key question in Praxis (`OPENQUESTIONS.md` Q1). A signature would let anyone confirm a badge came from us.\n- **Where the generator lives.** As before, the real one belongs in Descartes, and the prototype script isn't committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1611,"cache_read_input_tokens":221338,"output_tokens":667,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1611,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":667,"cache_read_input_tokens":221338,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1611,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1611},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"03c92b8a-44eb-4116-9aae-e63c96e16f97","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgizquMB15JDbVnjzg18q","requestRef":"a88850ce-3332-4434-ad38-a1238da92f31","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"6dbde9aa-dff5-4313-9985-1f4f995bfc53","timestamp":"2026-11-05T02:32:53.336Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc","sessionId":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","version":"2.1.317","gitBranch":"ec-ai-corpus","slug":"calm-crunching-lovelace"}
